Tech shares rallied on the first day of trading in 2018 Tuesday with shares of chipmakers and software publishers leading the charge. The tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite Index rose 1.3%, outpacing the 0.6% gain on the S&P 500 Index and the 0.2% rise in the Dow Jones Industrial Average . The PHLX Semiconductor Index rallied 2.1%, led by a 6.4% jump in shares of Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (AMD) and a 4.8% surge in Micron Technology Inc. (MU) shares. Other chipmakers with notable gains were Nvidia Corp. (NVDA), up 2.1%, Broadcom Ltd. (AVGO), up 3.3%, and Teradyne Inc. (TER), up 5.1%. Notable software gains included Electronic Arts Inc. (EA), up 4%, Symantec Corp. (SYMC), up 2.7%, and Salesforce.com Inc. (CRM), up 2.2%. Other big tech movers included Netflix Inc. (NFLX), up 5%, and Alibaba Group Holding Inc. (BABA), up 5.8%, while shares of Facebook Inc. (FB) rose 2.7%, and shares of Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL)(GOOGL) and Apple Inc. (AAPL) were up nearly 2%.
-Wallace Witkowski;
 1816ET
